# Working with Speko

Speko is two hosts with two non-interchangeable keys. Getting this wrong is the single most
common cause of a 401 that looks like an outage.

| Host | What it serves | Key | Base URL |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Router | STT, LLM, TTS — one request, benchmark-routed | `SPEKO_API_KEY` (`sk_...`) | `https://api.speko.ai/v1` |
| Platform | Agents, sessions, phone numbers, calls, knowledge bases, evals | `SPEKO_PLATFORM_API_KEY` (`sk_live_...`) | `https://api.speko.dev/v1` |

A key for one host returns 401 on the other. Keys are environment-scoped, so a staging key
fails against production. The hosted MCP at `mcp.speko.ai` speaks the platform side and
rejects a router key outright — it wants OAuth or a platform key.

## Rules

- Prefer the `speko` skill for transcription, synthesis and routing; prefer the Speko MCP
  tools for anything that creates, deploys, inspects or bills an agent.
- Never hardcode a vendor. `model: "auto"` routes on measured benchmarks; pin a model only
  when the user names one, and only from a `routable: true` row of `GET /v1/models`.
- Justify a routing choice with `GET /v1/routing/preview` before spending. It costs nothing
  and returns the pick, the reason, and the benchmark window behind it.
- Always request `response_format: "wav"` from `/v1/audio/speech`. The default is headerless
  24 kHz PCM that no player opens, and mp3 is refused before any upstream call.
- Read the `x-route` response header rather than assuming a pin won.
- Placing a phone call is irreversible and billed. Confirm the E.164 number, the purpose and
  the local hour with the user before dialing, every time. See the `speko-calls` skill.
- Read keys from the environment. Never inline one into a command that gets logged.
